.TH KAGI-VOLUME-HYPERVISOR-NOTES 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-hypervisor-notes \- show guest storage attachment options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-volume-hypervisor-notes
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints integration notes without creating a device or changing a VM.
Use the notes to choose the guest's virtual SCSI controller and Kagi's
backing transport independently.
.TP
.B KVM and QEMU
Use a live NBD backend with virtio-SCSI or an emulated LSI SAS controller.
.TP
.B VMware
Present an iSCSI LUN as appropriate for the VM or datastore.
Select the VMware Paravirtual SCSI (PVSCSI) controller in ESXi.
.TP
.B Hyper-V
Use an iSCSI LUN for SAN attachment or export a separate VHDX image.
Select the synthetic SCSI controller in Hyper-V.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-volume-qemu-scsi (1),
.BR kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi (1),
.BR kagi-volume-iscsi-export (1),
.BR kagi-volume-image (1)
